※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5005 LANG_STMT_VALUE_DISCARDED

※ '=' does not assign; it compares.  So this line asks whether 'status' is five
※ and then throws the answer away, which is what the habit every other language
※ teaches turns into here -- and it is reported rather than silently obeyed.
※ The last statement of a body is the function's result, so a comparison there
※ is the point of the line and is not reported; this one is not the last.
@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let status: mut = 3u8
    status = 5u8
    status
